# @plurnk/plurnk — the CLI/TUI client. Owned prefix: PLURNK_CLIENT_* (ecosystem
# standard: every package ships its knobs; this file IS the documentation).
# The client loads this itself, set-if-unset, beneath project/user env files and
# shell exports. The daemon owns its address, model, and provider keys; inspect
# their complete owner-labelled catalog with `plurnk-service config defaults`.

# Resume a workspace by name, or create it (rooted at cwd) if none exists.
# Unset = a fresh auto-named workspace per invocation ("cli" one-shot / "tui" REPL).
# PLURNK_CLIENT_WORKSPACE=

# Resume (or create) a named worker — the CONVERSATION — within that workspace.
# Requires PLURNK_CLIENT_WORKSPACE. Unset = the workspace's default conversation.
# PLURNK_CLIENT_WORKER=

# Absolute path passed as the workspace's project root at creation (the workspace
# for file ops). Unset = the editor/shell cwd. Empty string = explicitly headless.
# The root is decided at creation, permanently — changing it is unimplemented by design.
# PLURNK_CLIENT_PROJECT_ROOT=

# 1 = auto-accept every proposal locally without prompting; 0 = review each one.
# A prompt that starts with `?` is reviewed regardless.
PLURNK_CLIENT_YOLO=1

# 1 = nobody is attending: every loop is stated unattended, so the daemon offers no
# human-in-the-loop surface and settles proposals as its own panel says. 0 = say nothing.
PLURNK_CLIENT_AUTO=0

# What every loop does with a proposal: review | accept | reject. Unset = say nothing;
# the daemon's panel decides. A `?` prompt states review for that loop.
# PLURNK_CLIENT_PROPOSALS=

# CapabilityPolicy JSON applied when this client creates a workspace. Existing
# workspaces retain their durable setting.
# PLURNK_CLIENT_WORKSPACE_CAPABILITIES={}

# Truthy = one-shot runs emit the complete json record document on stdout (--json).
# PLURNK_CLIENT_JSON=
